---
/**
 * Privacy Policy (EN) — /privacy/
 *
 * Discloses:
 *   1. 100% Local Whisper Processing guarantee for the LiveAudio desktop app
 *   2. Microsoft Clarity integration (heatmaps, session replay, _clck, _clsk, privacy statement link)
 *   3. Vercel Analytics & Speed Insights
 *   4. Data rights and contact information
 */
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { localizedPath } from "../i18n/routes";

const path = localizedPath("en", "privacy");
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy — LiveAudio"
  description="Privacy Policy for LiveAudio and liveaudio.opencohost.com. Learn about our 100% local audio processing architecture, website analytics, and Microsoft Clarity integration."
  eyebrow="COMPLIANCE · LEGAL"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lastUpdated="Last updated: October 2026"
  badge="100% LOCAL PROCESSING"
  lang="en"
  path={path}
>
  <div class="callout-signal">
    <h3>
      <span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      100% Local Audio Processing Guarantee
    </h3>
    <p>
      LiveAudio is engineered from the ground up as a <strong>local-first desktop application</strong>.
      All speech recognition, audio capture, and Whisper AI inference execute strictly on your device's
      local hardware (CPU or CUDA/Vulkan GPU). <strong>No audio, speech, or transcription data is ever sent to,
      relayed through, or stored on external cloud servers, remote APIs, or third-party databases.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Overview and Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how Plynte Labs ("we", "us", or "our") handles information in connection with:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The LiveAudio Desktop Application:</strong> The downloadable software for Windows and Linux that provides
      real-time Whisper captions via local WebSocket.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The LiveAudio Website:</strong> The marketing and documentation site hosted at <code>liveaudio.opencohost.com</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. LiveAudio Desktop Application</h2>
  <p>
    The LiveAudio desktop software does not collect, record, transmit, or monetize your personal information or audio streams:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Zero Audio Transmission:</strong> Audio captured from your microphone or desktop loopback is processed
      in memory on your machine and immediately discarded after transcription frames are generated.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local Model Inference:</strong> Whisper model weights (e.g., GGML / GGUF binaries) are stored on your local
      drive and run entirely on local processor cores or graphics accelerators.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local-Only WebSocket:</strong> LiveAudio broadcasts transcription events over a local WebSocket server
      binding by default to <code>127.0.0.1:8765</code>. This connection is strictly local to your workstation and is never exposed
      to the public internet unless you explicitly configure remote network tunneling on your own infrastructure.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No Telemetry or Phone-Home:</strong> The application does not contain background analytics trackers, usage telemetry,
      or automated crash-reporting daemons that send data to our servers.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Website Information Collection & Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    When you browse <code>liveaudio.opencohost.com</code>, we collect limited usage metrics to monitor site performance,
    diagnose broken links, and optimize documentation. We do not require account registration, and we do not collect personal
    identifiers like names, physical addresses, or financial details.
  </p>

  <h3>Microsoft Clarity Integration</h3>
  <p>
    We partner with Microsoft Clarity and Microsoft Advertising to capture how you use and interact with our website through
    behavioral metrics, heatmaps, and session replay to improve and market our products and services. Website usage data is
    captured using first- and third-party cookies and other tracking technologies to determine the popularity of products and services
    and online activity. Additionally, we use this information for site optimization, fraud and security purposes, and advertising.
  </p>
  <p>
    Microsoft Clarity sets the following first-party cookies in your browser:
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Cookie</th>
          <th>Provider</th>
          <th>Duration</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_clck</code></td>
          <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
          <td>1 year</td>
          <td>Persists the unique Clarity user ID and browser settings across page navigation on the same domain.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_clsk</code></td>
          <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
          <td>1 day</td>
          <td>Connects individual page views into a single recorded session and tracks user interaction flow.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Clarity records user interactions such as mouse clicks, mouse movements, scrolling, and aggregate viewport dimensions.
    Sensitive text inputs and confidential form fields are automatically masked by Clarity prior to transmission.
    For more details on how Microsoft collects and processes your data, please review the
    <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Vercel Analytics & Speed Insights</h3>
  <p>
    Our website uses Vercel Analytics and Speed Insights to measure aggregate Core Web Vitals (such as Largest Contentful Paint,
    Interaction to Next Paint, and Cumulative Layout Shift) and page delivery performance. Vercel Analytics is designed to be privacy-preserving:
    it operates without persistent tracking cookies, does not collect personal data, and processes visitor requests using temporary,
    anonymized IP hashes.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cookies & Tracking Management</h2>
  <p>
    You can manage, restrict, or delete cookies at any time through your web browser preferences. Most modern browsers allow you to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Block third-party cookies or all cookies altogether.</li>
    <li>Delete existing cookies upon closing your browser session.</li>
    <li>Use private browsing or incognito windows to prevent long-term tracking.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can also learn how to opt out of Microsoft personalized advertising by visiting the
    <a href="https://account.microsoft.com/privacy/ad-settings" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Ad Settings page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data Retention & Security</h2>
  <p>
    Aggregated website analytics data is retained in accordance with Microsoft Clarity's standard data retention policies
    (typically 30 to 90 days for session recordings). We protect the website infrastructure using strict Content-Security-Policy (CSP) headers,
    enforced HTTPS encryption (TLS 1.3), and immutable asset hashing.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Open Source Code Transparency</h2>
  <p>
    Because LiveAudio is an open-source project licensed under the MIT License, our application code is publicly auditable.
    You can inspect the entire audio pipeline, WebSocket server implementation, and Whisper inference engine in our
    <a href="https://github.com/plynte-labs/LiveAudio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository</a>
    to verify that no audio or private telemetry leaves your computer.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on your location (including the European Economic Area, the UK, and California), you may have rights under applicable data protection
    laws (such as GDPR or CCPA/CPRA), including the right to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal data collected about you.
    Because we do not store customer profiles or collect identifiable personal records on our site, we may require additional contextual information
    to identify any relevant anonymized analytics records.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions, feedback, or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy or our local-first privacy practices, please contact us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@opencohost.com">contact@opencohost.com</a></li>
    <li><strong>Project Issues:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/plynte-labs/LiveAudio/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/plynte-labs/LiveAudio/issues</a></li>
    <li><strong>Organization:</strong> Plynte Labs</li>
  </ul>
</LegalPage>
